{#- targum Connect: targum in Claude, ChatGPT and the other assistants (targum-internal#80,
    remade 2026-09-24, and as boards ConnConnect and ConnConnectPhone draw it since
    2026-10-09: design.md §12, "The connector's pages are the boards'").

    One page for everyone. A signed-in reader meets it in the app's shell, the bar and
    the foot of every desk page; a stranger in the public bar, told once that connecting
    needs an account, with "New to targum?" and the waitlist at the close.

    **Note 2 is still the design of the steps: assume it is their first install.** Every
    app has its own tab with its own steps, and nothing is detected or guessed. The tabs
    are the reader's choice, and with JavaScript off every app's steps stand one under the
    other. The tab chosen names the app in the heading and in the small approval page.

    Baked in like every public page: no script, stylesheet or font off the network
    (§11), and its only pictures are three library covers from our own `/cover/` (§12,
    "A card's picture comes from targum.page"). `connect.js` switches the tabs and copies
    the address. Nothing here needs it. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
{% include '_public_head.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('landing-classic.css') }}{{ asset('connect.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
{{ chrome_face() }}
</head>
<body class="landing connect">
<header class="bar">
  <div class="col">
    <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="targum">
      <svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="20 12 56 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <rect x="20" y="12" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="currentColor"></rect>
        <rect x="54" y="22" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="var(--mark-accent)"></rect>
      </svg>
      targum
    </a>
    <nav class="places" aria-label="{{ t("connect.page.on-this-page", "On this page") }}">
      <a href="#install">{{ t("connect.page.set-it-up", "Set it up") }}</a>
      <a href="#why">{{ t("connect.page.what-you-get", "What you get") }}</a>
      <a href="#questions">{{ t("connect.page.faq", "FAQ") }}</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="end">
      <p class="tongue">
        {%- if page_language == 'ru' %}<a href="/connect?lang=en" hreflang="en">EN</a><span>/</span><b>RU</b>
        {%- else %}<b>EN</b><span>/</span><a href="/connect?lang=ru" hreflang="ru">RU</a>{% endif %}
      </p>
      <a class="signin" href="/account/signin">{{ t("connect.page.sign-in", "Sign in") }}</a>
      <a class="btn cta small" href="#install">{{ t("connect.page.connect-targum", "Connect targum") }}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

{% include '_connect_body.html.j2' %}

{% with signin = true %}{% include '_public_foot.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}
{% if strings %}<script>window.TARGUM_STRINGS = {{ strings|tojson }};</script>
{% endif %}<script>{{ asset('strings.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('connect.js') }}</script>
</body>
</html>
